From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 07:57:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] am335x: guard board MAC setup when net is disabled

The tiny BeagleBone Optimal boot contract disables U-Boot networking. Keep
the AM335x board late init path available, but skip the Ethernet MAC
environment setup when the network stack is not built.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [project-specific BeagleBone Optimal Tiny boot contract]
Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 board/ti/am335x/board.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/ti/am335x/board.c b/board/ti/am335x/board.c
index 34f987c2b72..656fc58fd8d 100644
--- a/board/ti/am335x/board.c
+++ b/board/ti/am335x/board.c
@@ -799,7 +799,7 @@ int board_init(void)
 int board_late_init(void)
 {
 	struct udevice *dev;
-#if !defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD)
+#if !defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) && CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(NET)
 	uint8_t mac_addr[6];
 	uint32_t mac_hi, mac_lo;
 #endif
@@ -848,7 +848,7 @@ int board_late_init(void)
 		env_set("boot_fit", "1");
 #endif
 
-#if !defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD)
+#if !defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD) && CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(NET)
 	/* try reading mac address from efuse */
 	mac_lo = readl(&cdev->macid0l);
 	mac_hi = readl(&cdev->macid0h);
-- 
2.34.1

